%I A399461 #13 Sep 13 2026 00:31:46
%S A399461 1,0,1,1,1,0,2,0,2,1,3,1,2,1,13,1,5,21,235
%N A399461 Number of Chvátal-Erdős graphs with order n.
%C A399461 A Chvátal-Erdős graph is triangle-free with independence number and connectivity both equal. This implies that it is regular and has diameter 2.
%C A399461 Column sums of table in A399459.
%H A399461 Allan Bickle, Megan Cream and Ron Gould, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.disc.2026.115336">Chorded cycles in Chvátal-Erdős graphs</a>, Discrete Math, 350 (2027), 115336.
%H A399461 A. F. Sidorenko, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/0012-365X(91)90114-H">Triangle-free regular graphs</a>, Discrete Math., 91 (1991), 215-217.
%F A399461 a(n) > 0 for n > 9.
%e A399461 For n=2, the only graph is K_2.
%e A399461 For n=4, the only graph is C_4.
%e A399461 For n=5, the only graph is C_5.
%e A399461 For n=6, the only graph is K_3,3.
%e A399461 For n=8, the two graphs are M_8 and K_4,4.
%e A399461 For n=10, the two graphs are C_10 (1,4) and K_5,5.
%e A399461 For n=11, the only graph is C_11 (1,3).
%e A399461 For n=12, the three graphs are C_12 (2,3), the Chvátal graph, and K_6,6.
%e A399461 For n=13, the only graph is C_13 (1,5).
%e A399461 For n=14, the two graphs are C_14 (1,4,7) and K_7,7.
%e A399461 For n=15, the only graph is C_15 (1,4,6).
%Y A399461 Cf. A399459 (table for order n and degree d).
%Y A399461 Cf. A399460 (degree d).
%K A399461 nonn,more,new
%O A399461 2,7
%A A399461 _Allan Bickle_, Aug 29 2026
%E A399461 a(18) from _Sean A. Irvine_, Sep 06 2026
%E A399461 a(19) and a(20) from _Allan Bickle_, Sep 10 2026
